                "catalogCode": "CHC-m0ck00007783",
                "internalName": "Attachments Submission",
                "marketingTitle": "",
                "tagline": "",
                "toolTipDescription": "",
                "shortDescription": "",
                "longDescription": "<p>The <strong>Attachments Submission</strong> API supports the X12 EDI 275 Patient Information transaction. It translates this standard to JSON, so it is more accessible to developers for integration into users&rsquo; applications.<br/>Submissions take two forms:</p><ul><li>Solicited &ndash; usually sent by a payer to a provider requesting documentation for a claim</li><li>Unsolicited &ndash; ex. Workman&rsquo;s Compensation</li></ul><p>An attachment, in the context of healthcare electronic data interchange (EDI), is an electronic rendition of medical documentation, such as an X-ray, lab report, or questionnaire, to support a healthcare administrative transaction. Our Attachment solution includes workers&rsquo; compensation attachments and medical attachments. Any receiver who does not support electronic attachments will receive the documentation through fax or mail.</p>",
